---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Ava from '@src/assets/img/ava.jpg';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';

---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Me"
  description="About Bhupesh, a Computer Engineering student interested in databases, C++, systems programming, and computer science."
>
  <div class="container">
    <main class="prose text-lg dark:prose-invert">
      <article>
        <div class="w-full md:flex md:items-center gap-16 mb-10">
          <div class="text-pretty leading-9">
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">
              Hi, I'm Bhupesh.
            </h1>

            <Prose>
              <div class="text-lg">
                <p>
                  I am a Computer Engineering student interested in
                  database systems, C++, systems programming, and computer
                  science.
                </p>

                <p>
                  I enjoy understanding how software works beneath the
                  surface and building things from the ground up. My current
                  work includes <strong>BinaryDB</strong>, a minimal
                  page-based NoSQL document database built in C++.
                </p>
              </div>
            </Prose>
          </div>

          <Image
            src={Ava}
            alt="Bhupesh"
            width={300}
            class="rounded-3xl rotate-3 mx-4 md:mx-0"
          />
        </div>

        <h2>What I Work On</h2>

        <p>
          My main interests are around systems and the software that sits
          underneath applications. I particularly enjoy learning about
          database internals, storage engines, operating systems, and
          low-level programming.
        </p>

        <h2>Technical Interests</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>Database systems and storage engines</li>
          <li>C++ and systems programming</li>
          <li>Operating systems</li>
          <li>Data structures and algorithms</li>
          <li>Computer networks and distributed systems</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What I'm Currently Learning</h2>

        <p>
          I'm continuously strengthening my foundations in computer science
          while building practical projects. I use projects as a way to turn
          theoretical concepts into working software.
        </p>

        <p>
          I'm particularly interested in understanding how databases store,
          retrieve, organize, and manage data efficiently.
        </p>

        <h2>Beyond the Code</h2>

        <p>
          I also write about the things I learn. My blog is a collection of
          notes, experiments, technical explanations, and lessons from
          building projects.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you're interested in databases, systems programming, or
          computer science, feel free to explore my
          <a href="/projects/">projects</a> or read my
          <a href="/posts/">blog</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>